      "local": "where [MATH] is the restoring force, [MATH] is the displacement from equilibrium or deformation, and [MATH] is the spring constant of the system.",
      "upstream": "where [MATH] is the restoring force, [MATH] is the displacement from equilibrium or deformation, and [MATH] is the force constant of the system.",
      "local_html": "where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow /></mrow></mrow></math> is the restoring force, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow /></mrow></mrow></math> is the displacement from equilibrium or deformation, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow /></mrow></mrow></math> is the spring constant of the system. ",
      "upstream_html": "where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow></math> is the restoring force, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></math> is the displacement from equilibrium or deformation, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></math> is the force constant of the system. ",
